                        "entry_id": "ac41edd0-8461-3707-b166-52aa38ed6c60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An attendee; one who attends a course, meeting, school, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "27fe6f2e-8a22-4161-ba3c-11b267f48de9",
                                "sense_id": "8ccfb206-d45e-3a32-81ea-740a8f4dbc6b",
                                "text": "She was a very constant attender of First-day and week-day meetings, at the meeting places she belonged to"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d6b6044-6ae2-49b6-be4c-7d56fdf0cdcc",
                                "sense_id": "8ccfb206-d45e-3a32-81ea-740a8f4dbc6b",
                                "text": "1900, James Wideman Lee, Naphtali Luccock, and James Main Dixon, The Illustrated History of Methodism, page 345, The Methodist Magazine Publishing Co.\nAnd she continued her infamous trade of procuress, while a zealous and regular attender of the Tabernacle at Tottenham-Court!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45bd46ef-7c3e-432d-8d62-db05fb6b7591",
                                "sense_id": "8ccfb206-d45e-3a32-81ea-740a8f4dbc6b",
                                "text": "The great distance that some youth travel...is bound to play its part in the case of the borderline student who becomes an infrequent attender and finally drops out of school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a81cb36-5763-412a-866c-13b784155cfe",
                                "sense_id": "8ccfb206-d45e-3a32-81ea-740a8f4dbc6b",
                                "text": "If there is no spiritual distinction between member and attender, the question is asked, Why have membership at all?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a0d6ac4-e938-39f1-874c-361160b5a954",
                        "entry_id": "ac41edd0-8461-3707-b166-52aa38ed6c60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An attendant; one who attends to someone or something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c83f21ef-80c1-4af5-b8af-b360b41672eb",
                                "sense_id": "7a0d6ac4-e938-39f1-874c-361160b5a954",
                                "text": "Sri C. Rajabather was appointed to assist in the office as typist attender from 7-4-41."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "790c8f61-134c-398c-8e72-e6a8bedd6291",
                        "entry_id": "ac41edd0-8461-3707-b166-52aa38ed6c60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The subject; one who experiences."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca86a76b-f0ce-4929-b56e-354dcd89a461",
                                "sense_id": "790c8f61-134c-398c-8e72-e6a8bedd6291",
                                "text": "the whole process of ages’-long mentalization, of which our present ability of conceiving “Mind” forms only the culmination, and by no means the constant attender."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9953a7ad-83d9-4965-bb1f-1f7aa3deb5db",
                                "sense_id": "790c8f61-134c-398c-8e72-e6a8bedd6291",
                                "text": "Activity of attention for the sake of knowledge changes only the mind of the attender and is resisted only by the habits, biases, laziness and the like"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4475ca4b-f337-47f0-9bca-85d3e34aef28",
                                "sense_id": "790c8f61-134c-398c-8e72-e6a8bedd6291",
                                "text": "The other aspect pertains to the subject’s own subjectivity, those qualities that constitute the subject as the experiencer or attender."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
